WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:11.100
Langley argued in 1905 that nicotine and curare act on a receptive substance in the

2
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.240
muscle cell itself.

3
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.640
Nobody could isolate or count it.

4
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.760
Until binding was measured, a receptor could only be inferred from a response, such

5
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.780
as a contraction in an organ bath.

6
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.280
And a response is not the same as occupancy.

7
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:33.620
So how many sites does a tissue hold, and how tightly does a ligand hold them?

8
00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.033
Take membranes that hold the receptor.

9
00:00:38.013 --> 00:00:42.373
Add a ligand made radioactive but still biologically active.

10
00:00:43.393 --> 00:00:46.433
Incubate until binding and release are equal.

11
00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:53.253
That is equilibrium, where Kd is ligand times receptor, over the complex.

12
00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.613
Tight binders take longer.

13
00:00:56.867 --> 00:01:00.347
Pull the mixture through a filter that traps the membranes.

14
00:01:00.967 --> 00:01:04.307
Wash it several times, so unbound label goes.

15
00:01:05.227 --> 00:01:06.807
Count the radioactivity left.

16
00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.847
That is total binding.

17
00:01:09.807 --> 00:01:15.007
Repeat with a large excess of unlabelled ligand, which competes the label off the

18
00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:16.167
finite receptor sites.

19
00:01:16.807 --> 00:01:19.507
What still counts is nonspecific binding.

20
00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:23.507
Total minus nonspecific is specific binding.

21
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.940
In saturation, raise the labelled ligand.

22
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:34.900
Specific binding levels off at the number of sites, Bmax, and is half-maximal at

23
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:41.540
Kd. In competition, hold the label fixed and add rising unlabelled compound.

24
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:48.620
Its Ki is calculated from the IC50, the concentration that halves binding, with the

25
00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:49.720
Cheng-Prusoff correction.

26
00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:52.723
An idealised example.

27
00:01:53.863 --> 00:02:02.923
0.80 mg of protein binds 66 fmol in total, and 18 with a 100-fold excess of

28
00:02:02.923 --> 00:02:04.243
unlabelled estradiol.

29
00:02:05.523 --> 00:02:10.363
Specific binding is 48, so 60 fmol of receptor per mg.

30
00:02:11.763 --> 00:02:17.063
Across concentrations, nonspecific binding usually keeps rising, while specific

31
00:02:17.063 --> 00:02:18.423
binding saturates.

32
00:02:19.283 --> 00:02:26.183
10% to 90% occupancy takes an 81-fold rise in ligand, so the axis is logarithmic.

33
00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.767
Binding is not response.

34
00:02:29.587 --> 00:02:33.007
A tissue can give a full response with most receptors empty.

35
00:02:33.907 --> 00:02:39.307
These spare receptors can put the EC50, the concentration giving half the maximum

36
00:02:39.307 --> 00:02:41.287
response, below Kd.

37
00:02:42.387 --> 00:02:44.907
So measure Kd by binding and compare.

38
00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:50.687
If receptors take up much of the label, curves steepen, so keep depletion under

39
00:02:50.687 --> 00:02:56.547
about 10%. Too short an incubation distorts curves, so measure the time course.

40
00:02:57.367 --> 00:03:02.687
Lefkowitz and colleagues made radioactive ACTH in 1970.

41
00:03:03.827 --> 00:03:09.467
Adrenal extracts bound it, and unlabelled ACTH and five derivatives inhibited

42
00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:12.647
binding in proportion to their biological activity.

43
00:03:13.647 --> 00:03:19.487
In 1973 Pert and Snyder used tritiated naloxone on rat brain.

44
00:03:20.727 --> 00:03:26.507
Binding was saturable, with a Kd of 20 nM and a density of 30 pmol/g.

45
00:03:26.507 --> 00:03:31.487
Fifteen opiates and antagonists competed for the same sites.

46
00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.840
A binding site for a plant drug strengthened the case that the brain makes its own

47
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:46.280
opioids. In 1975 Hughes, Kosterlitz and colleagues identified two pentapeptides, the

48
00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:53.700
enkephalins. In 1974 Brown and Goldstein found that normal fibroblasts bound

49
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:59.400
labelled LDL with high affinity, but cells from five homozygous subjects with

50
00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.020
familial hypercholesterolemia did not.

51
00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:07.060
The binding defect may account for the cells' cholesterol overproduction.

52
00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:13.180
Binding counts sites and measures grip; a response is not occupancy.
